      "content": "I understand your position on the inherent value of all dialects. Let me rephrase to be more precise for our administrative planning. Rather than discussing intelligence, can we look at this from a sociolinguistic perspective regarding \"linguistic code-switching\"? \n\nSpecifically, in a high-rigor environment that relies heavily on Standard Academic English (SAE), is there documented research suggesting that students who primarily utilize non-standard dialects face a higher \"cognitive load\" when attempting to adhere to the rigid syntactical and grammatical structures required in advanced composition? We are trying to determine if the necessity of constant code-switching might impact a student's ability to focus on complex subject matter compared to students for whom SAE is their primary, natural mode of thought.",
